WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.807
Sovereign AI means practical control over AI capability.

2
00:00:03.807 --> 00:00:10.645
In this course, it is not a vague political slogan and it is not limited to running a model on a local laptop.

3
00:00:10.645 --> 00:00:26.030
A sovereign AI program gives an organization deliberate control over where data goes, which models are approved, who can use them, what tools they can access, how outputs are reviewed, how logs are handled, and how changes are governed.

4
00:00:26.030 --> 00:00:29.837
Public AI tools can be useful for many low-risk workflows.

5
00:00:29.837 --> 00:00:40.716
Private AI systems may be necessary when data sensitivity, customer commitments, regulatory expectations, or operational ownership require tighter boundaries.

6
00:00:40.716 --> 00:00:51.982
Hybrid patterns may be the most realistic path for many teams, routing different work to local, private, or approved managed services based on data class and business need.

7
00:00:51.982 --> 00:00:54.158
The key idea is informed control.

8
00:00:54.158 --> 00:01:03.793
Teams need to understand the data, the model, the runtime, the access layer, the retrieval system, the monitoring plan, and the operational owner.

9
00:01:03.793 --> 00:01:15.992
Without that understanding, a system may feel private while still exposing sensitive prompts through logs, unmanaged embeddings, broad tool permissions, or unclear vendor settings.

10
00:01:15.992 --> 00:01:20.576
Sovereign AI is therefore an engineering and governance discipline.

11
00:01:20.576 --> 00:01:27.259
It combines infrastructure, security, privacy, policy, cost management, and user workflow design.

12
00:01:27.259 --> 00:01:30.211
The goal is not to make every system isolated.

13
00:01:30.211 --> 00:01:35.573
The goal is to make every AI workflow intentional, reviewable, and maintainable.
